401
00:29:28,090 --> 00:29:31,750
And then do keep in mind,
this is another node module.

402
00:29:31,750 --> 00:29:35,490
So let's go ahead and copy that.

403
00:29:35,490 --> 00:29:38,350
And going to kill
the metro server.

404
00:29:38,350 --> 00:29:40,550
Anytime you install
a new node module,

405
00:29:40,550 --> 00:29:43,690
you will need to
stop and restart

406
00:29:43,690 --> 00:29:45,830
your metro bundler anyway.

407
00:29:51,765 --> 00:29:56,530
And then NPM start that
back up again and let's

408
00:29:56,530 --> 00:30:00,510
go grab that code, copy.

409
00:30:06,370 --> 00:30:10,210
And then we should see
our import statements.

410
00:30:10,210 --> 00:30:14,490
We don't have as many things
imported from React Native

411
00:30:14,490 --> 00:30:16,890
anymore.

412
00:30:16,890 --> 00:30:17,950
Just a view.

413
00:30:17,950 --> 00:30:21,760
View will always be
from React Native.

414
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:24,620
And then the FlatList
and StyleSheet component.

415
00:30:24,620 --> 00:30:27,640
Everything else is now--
all of our other UI elements

416
00:30:27,640 --> 00:30:31,900
are coming from React Native
paper, which is what you want.

417
00:30:31,900 --> 00:30:33,820
If you're going to
use a design system,

418
00:30:33,820 --> 00:30:36,420
you want to use it in as
many places as possible.

419
00:30:36,420 --> 00:30:40,240
You don't want to mix like React
Native paper text component

420
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:44,140
with a React Native text
component in the same page.

421
00:30:44,140 --> 00:30:46,680
You want to be consistent.

