509
00:37:17,850 --> 00:37:21,450
One other thing
that we need to do

510
00:37:21,450 --> 00:37:28,410
if you're using React Native
paper is to use a provider.

511
00:37:28,410 --> 00:37:31,850
So if we pop over
to our layout.jsx,

512
00:37:31,850 --> 00:37:36,350
and I actually already put this
in there, but I'll revert this.

513
00:37:36,350 --> 00:37:38,930
So it's like it was before.

514
00:37:38,930 --> 00:37:42,570
We just had a route
layout that was returning

515
00:37:42,570 --> 00:37:46,850
a stack that rendered--

516
00:37:46,850 --> 00:37:52,570
this automatically renders our
index component by default.

517
00:37:52,570 --> 00:37:56,370
What a provider
is, is it provides

518
00:37:56,370 --> 00:38:00,610
context for, in this
case, React Native paper.

519
00:38:00,610 --> 00:38:03,930
And what that's doing is any
component that you end up

520
00:38:03,930 --> 00:38:09,120
rendering in your app,
any page or any component

521
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:12,320
inside those pages will
all be able to have access

522
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:15,160
to the same theme context.

523
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:20,360
React Native paper has a
light theme by default.

524
00:38:20,360 --> 00:38:25,360
But if you wrap your app
in this paper provider

525
00:38:25,360 --> 00:38:30,400
and then you want to use
the React Native paper theme

526
00:38:30,400 --> 00:38:33,960
settings to change your accent
colors or your light or dark

527
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:38,360
theme, then the entire
component or the entire app

528
00:38:38,360 --> 00:38:40,880
will be able to
have access to that

529
00:38:40,880 --> 00:38:46,400
without you having to update
every one programmatically.

530
00:38:46,400 --> 00:38:53,520
We'll use providers again later
in Expo projects or any React

531
00:38:53,520 --> 00:38:55,600
or React Native project.

532
00:38:55,600 --> 00:38:57,640
Specifically, we're
going to use one

533
00:38:57,640 --> 00:39:02,120
for Redux, which I've
talked about previously.

534
00:39:02,120 --> 00:39:06,300
That is just a global
state management solution,

535
00:39:06,300 --> 00:39:09,560
and we'll need a provider so
that all of our components

536
00:39:09,560 --> 00:39:14,360
can have access to
that provider data.

537
00:39:14,360 --> 00:39:21,760
So go ahead and give this
a shot with your project.

